{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790450011,"nonce":"TagXOMC1BQUDacvBYC3LjPARiPI=","title":"Python records: read-only dynamic consumers still demote the shape","message":"The first cut of P-dict-records (ad42115) keeps a record only while every use is a literal build, a literal-key read or store of its shape, or a typed pass (locals, parameters, returns, lists, fields). Every other use the lowering meets demotes the shape and the program is typed again with its literals as dicts: a box (print, json.dumps, str/repr, f-strings, any Object slot), ==, `in`, len, iteration, keys/values/items/get, type/isinstance, attribute reads, a literal key outside the shape (the brief lowers a read of one to KeyError), and a builtin given the record. A compile error in a program that has records also demotes every shape.\n\nStill owed from the brief: per-record zb_hook_instance_str/eq/json/getitem arms so a record can be boxed, with the whole-program gate (Module.dynamic_dict_mutation) that makes that sound; constant len/in/iteration and get as the field joined with the default; display_name \"dict\" in every message; KeyError(repr(lit)) for a literal key outside the shape. json_bench's literals demote today (json.dumps boxes them), so it pays a second typing pass; a demotion found in the entry body pays a full second lowering.","files":null}]}